                {
                  "id": "F-001",
                  "title": "[F-001] SQL injection in product search",
                  "type": "Tampering",
                  "status": "Open",
                  "severity": "Critical",
                  "description": "The search handler builds SQL with a template literal from the untrusted `q` parameter.\n\nImpact: An attacker reads the full product and order tables and can write arbitrary rows.\n\nRisk: Critical (likelihood High, impact Critical)\nCWE: CWE-89\nCVSS v4: 9.3 (CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N)\nEvidence tier: confirmed-exploitable\nSource: stride\n\nEvidence:\n`db.query(`SELECT * FROM products WHERE name LIKE '%${q}%'`)` at search.ts:42 concatenates the raw parameter.\n- src/api/search.ts:42\n\nTrust boundary crossings:\n- tb-2 external → rest-api (internet-facing): The perimeter assumes the query layer parameterizes untrusted input.\n\nFull finding: threat-model.md#f-001 (F-001)",
                  "mitigation": "M-001 — Parameterize the product search query (priority P1, effort Medium)\n1. Replace the template literal with a parameterized query.\n2. Add a lint rule that rejects string-built SQL.\nVerification: sqlmap reports no injectable parameter against /api/search.",
                  "modelType": "STRIDE",
                  "number": 1,
                  "score": "9.3"
                }
              ]
            }
